# Experiment protocol

`run.sh <run-dir> <seed>` is the fixed trusted entry point. The extension picks
`<run-dir>` under `/results/<uuid>`; the language model cannot select a shell
command or choose arbitrary output paths.

- Read source and datasets from `/project` (read-only Docker bind mount).
- Write `metrics.json`, logs, checkpoints, plots, and all temporary artifacts
  under the supplied run directory in `/results`.
- Use stable metric names and a fixed evaluation budget.
- Check numerical validity and correctness before recording an objective value.
- Run multiple seeds for promising configurations and compare variance.
- When using `uv` for project dependencies, keep `UV_PROJECT_ENVIRONMENT`
  and `UV_CACHE_DIR` pointed under `/results`; read-only project roots cannot
  host an automatically-created `.venv`.
- To customize the runtime, modify `.devcontainer/Dockerfile` in your regular
  development container and rebuild the Pi container.

The bundled `benchmark.py` counts Python source files only as an executable
smoke test. Replace it with your domain-specific evaluator.
